  {
    "episode_id": 76154,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76154.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 50,
    "turn_text": "It was a challenge of a lifetime and we knew it would be as fortunate because we had leaders on the Ways and Means Committee who had really driven us for years as a committee to be ready to do tax reform. Dave Camp would be a good example for six years. Paul Ryan, of course, who had long focused on reforming the tax code that I followed and then We had already put together the better way sort of Republican tax plan prior to President Trump coming into office. And so we had worked years and years to be ready for a president who would open that window and allow us to dive through it. And that's exactly what happened.",
